            <div xml:id="d1162">

                <pb facs="0828" n="712" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg712"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.6363/130.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Vice Consul Bevan.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 634.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-09-03">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 3, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department has received your despatch
                    No. 1182 of August 14, 1914, enclosing a copy of a decree issued by Governor
                    Candido Aguilar of the State of Vera Cruz, Mexico, relative to leasing oil lands
                    in the State of Vera Cruz. The Department presumes that the decree in question
                    is intended to relate to future transactions only. Inasmuch, however, as it does
                    not appear entirely clear from the language of the decree that such is the case,
                    you are directed to make an investigation and report on this point.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State: <lb/>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilbur J. Carr</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
